window.PARAPHRASE_DATA={"build":"2026.09.01-v77-band8-review","howTo":["Do not memorise advanced words as isolated synonyms. Learn the meaning, collocation, register, and a simple-English escape route.","For every entry, say the advanced word, then explain it without using that word. This trains retrieval and paraphrase at the same time.","In Speaking, if a word does not come within about one second, keep the idea and explain it in simpler English instead of stopping.","In Writing, prefer precision and natural collocation over rare vocabulary. A sophisticated word used inaccurately is worse than a simpler word used precisely.","No vocabulary list alone can guarantee Band 8 or 9. Official descriptors also require fluency/coherence, grammatical range/accuracy, pronunciation in Speaking, and task response/cohesion in Writing."],"vocab":[{"category":"Nouns","n":1,"word":"accountability","vi":"trách nhiệm giải trình","simple":"the responsibility to explain or justify your actions","example":"Greater accountability can improve public trust in large institutions."},{"category":"Nouns","n":2,"word":"adversity","vi":"nghịch cảnh","simple":"a difficult or unpleasant situation that tests your ability to cope","example":"People often discover their strengths when they face adversity."},{"category":"Nouns","n":3,"word":"ambiguity","vi":"sự mơ hồ","simple":"a lack of clarity that allows more than one interpretation","example":"The ambiguity of the policy caused unnecessary confusion."},{"category":"Nouns","n":4,"word":"aspiration","vi":"khát vọng","simple":"a strong hope or ambition to achieve something","example":"For many students, studying abroad is a long-term aspiration."},{"category":"Nouns","n":5,"word":"autonomy","vi":"quyền tự chủ","simple":"the freedom to make your own decisions","example":"Remote work can give employees greater autonomy over their schedules."},{"category":"Nouns","n":6,"word":"bias","vi":"thiên kiến","simple":"an unfair tendency to favour one side, person, or idea","example":"Hiring decisions should be designed to reduce unconscious bias."},{"category":"Nouns","n":7,"word":"burden","vi":"gánh nặng","simple":"a heavy responsibility, cost, or difficulty","example":"High housing costs place a serious burden on young families."},{"category":"Nouns","n":8,"word":"capacity","vi":"năng lực; khả năng","simple":"the ability or amount that someone or something can handle","example":"Public hospitals need more capacity to deal with an ageing population."},{"category":"Nouns","n":9,"word":"cohesion","vi":"sự gắn kết","simple":"the quality of being connected and working well together","example":"Community events can strengthen social cohesion."},{"category":"Nouns","n":10,"word":"commitment","vi":"sự cam kết","simple":"a strong decision to keep supporting or doing something","example":"Learning a language requires consistent effort and long-term commitment."},{"category":"Nouns","n":11,"word":"competence","vi":"năng lực","simple":"the ability to do something successfully","example":"Technical competence alone does not guarantee good leadership."},{"category":"Nouns","n":12,"word":"compromise","vi":"thỏa hiệp","simple":"an agreement in which each side accepts less than it originally wanted","example":"A workable compromise may be better than a perfect solution that no one accepts."},{"category":"Nouns","n":13,"word":"consensus","vi":"sự đồng thuận","simple":"general agreement among a group of people","example":"There is growing consensus that prevention is cheaper than treatment."},{"category":"Nouns","n":14,"word":"constraint","vi":"sự hạn chế; ràng buộc","simple":"a limit that restricts what can be done","example":"Time is often the biggest constraint for working adults."},{"category":"Nouns","n":15,"word":"controversy","vi":"sự tranh cãi","simple":"strong public disagreement about an issue","example":"The proposal has generated considerable controversy."},{"category":"Nouns","n":16,"word":"credibility","vi":"độ tin cậy","simple":"the quality of being trusted and believed","example":"A news outlet can quickly lose credibility if it publishes inaccurate information."},{"category":"Nouns","n":17,"word":"criterion","vi":"tiêu chí","simple":"a standard used to judge or decide something","example":"Salary should not be the only criterion when choosing a career."},{"category":"Nouns","n":18,"word":"decline","vi":"sự suy giảm","simple":"a gradual reduction in quality, quantity, or importance","example":"Many small towns have experienced a decline in population."},{"category":"Nouns","n":19,"word":"deterioration","vi":"sự xuống cấp; suy thoái","simple":"the process of becoming worse","example":"Sleep deprivation can lead to a deterioration in concentration."},{"category":"Nouns","n":20,"word":"dilemma","vi":"tình thế khó xử","simple":"a situation in which every available choice has disadvantages","example":"Governments face a dilemma between economic growth and environmental protection."},{"category":"Nouns","n":21,"word":"disparity","vi":"sự chênh lệch","simple":"a noticeable and often unfair difference","example":"There is still a significant disparity between urban and rural incomes."},{"category":"Nouns","n":22,"word":"disruption","vi":"sự gián đoạn; xáo trộn","simple":"a major interruption to the normal way something works","example":"Artificial intelligence is likely to cause disruption in some industries."},{"category":"Nouns","n":23,"word":"diversity","vi":"sự đa dạng","simple":"the presence of many different types of people, ideas, or things","example":"Cultural diversity can expose people to different ways of thinking."},{"category":"Nouns","n":24,"word":"efficiency","vi":"hiệu suất; hiệu quả","simple":"the ability to achieve a result without wasting time, money, or effort","example":"Automation can improve efficiency in routine administrative work."},{"category":"Nouns","n":25,"word":"exposure","vi":"sự tiếp xúc","simple":"the experience of coming into contact with something","example":"Regular exposure to English is essential for developing natural fluency."},{"category":"Nouns","n":26,"word":"flexibility","vi":"tính linh hoạt","simple":"the ability to change or adapt easily","example":"Working from home can give parents much greater flexibility in managing family responsibilities."},{"category":"Nouns","n":27,"word":"framework","vi":"khuôn khổ","simple":"a basic system or structure used to organise ideas or actions","example":"A clear legal framework is needed before the technology is widely adopted."},{"category":"Nouns","n":28,"word":"hardship","vi":"gian khó; khó khăn","simple":"serious difficulty, especially involving money or living conditions","example":"Unexpected medical bills can cause financial hardship."},{"category":"Nouns","n":29,"word":"incentive","vi":"động lực; sự khuyến khích","simple":"something that encourages a person to act","example":"Tax reductions can provide an incentive for companies to invest."},{"category":"Nouns","n":30,"word":"inclination","vi":"khuynh hướng","simple":"a natural preference or tendency to do something","example":"I have a strong inclination to plan things in advance."},{"category":"Nouns","n":31,"word":"inequality","vi":"sự bất bình đẳng","simple":"an unfair difference in opportunities, wealth, or treatment","example":"Education can reduce inequality, but only if access is genuinely broad."},{"category":"Nouns","n":32,"word":"infrastructure","vi":"cơ sở hạ tầng","simple":"the basic systems and facilities a society or organisation needs","example":"Reliable public transport depends on adequate infrastructure."},{"category":"Nouns","n":33,"word":"innovation","vi":"sự đổi mới","simple":"a new idea, method, or product that improves how something is done","example":"Competition can encourage innovation."},{"category":"Nouns","n":34,"word":"insight","vi":"sự thấu hiểu","simple":"a clear and deep understanding of something","example":"Living abroad gave me valuable insight into another culture."},{"category":"Nouns","n":35,"word":"integrity","vi":"tính chính trực","simple":"the quality of being honest and guided by strong principles","example":"Public officials are expected to act with integrity."},{"category":"Nouns","n":36,"word":"intervention","vi":"sự can thiệp","simple":"an action taken to improve or change a difficult situation","example":"Early intervention can prevent minor problems from becoming serious."},{"category":"Nouns","n":37,"word":"justification","vi":"sự biện minh; lý do chính đáng","simple":"a good reason that explains why something is acceptable","example":"There is little justification for wasting public money on unnecessary projects."},{"category":"Nouns","n":38,"word":"livelihood","vi":"sinh kế","simple":"the way a person earns enough money to live","example":"Automation may threaten the livelihoods of some low-skilled workers."},{"category":"Nouns","n":39,"word":"literacy","vi":"năng lực đọc hiểu; hiểu biết","simple":"the ability to understand and use information in a particular area","example":"Digital literacy is becoming as important as traditional literacy."},{"category":"Nouns","n":40,"word":"misconception","vi":"quan niệm sai lầm","simple":"an idea or belief that is incorrect","example":"A common misconception is that expensive products are always better."},{"category":"Nouns","n":41,"word":"obstacle","vi":"trở ngại","simple":"something that makes progress difficult","example":"Lack of confidence can be a major obstacle to speaking a foreign language."},{"category":"Nouns","n":42,"word":"outcome","vi":"kết quả","simple":"the final result of an action or situation","example":"Better preparation usually leads to a more positive outcome."},{"category":"Nouns","n":43,"word":"perspective","vi":"góc nhìn","simple":"a particular way of seeing or understanding something","example":"Travel can give people a broader perspective on their own society."},{"category":"Nouns","n":44,"word":"priority","vi":"ưu tiên","simple":"something considered more important than other things","example":"For me, maintaining good health is a higher priority than earning more money."},{"category":"Nouns","n":45,"word":"resilience","vi":"khả năng phục hồi","simple":"the ability to recover after difficulty or failure","example":"Resilience is particularly important in competitive careers."},{"category":"Nouns","n":46,"word":"scarcity","vi":"sự khan hiếm","simple":"a situation in which there is not enough of something","example":"Water scarcity is becoming a serious concern in many regions."},{"category":"Nouns","n":47,"word":"scrutiny","vi":"sự xem xét kỹ lưỡng","simple":"careful and detailed examination","example":"Public spending should be subject to close scrutiny."},{"category":"Nouns","n":48,"word":"sustainability","vi":"tính bền vững","simple":"the ability to continue for a long time without causing serious harm","example":"Long-term sustainability matters more than short-term profit."},{"category":"Nouns","n":49,"word":"tendency","vi":"xu hướng","simple":"a pattern of behaving or developing in a particular way","example":"There is a tendency for people to underestimate how much time they spend online."},{"category":"Nouns","n":50,"word":"trade-off","vi":"sự đánh đổi","simple":"a situation where gaining one advantage requires accepting a disadvantage","example":"There is often a trade-off between convenience and privacy."},{"category":"Nouns","n":51,"word":"vulnerability","vi":"tính dễ tổn thương","simple":"the state of being easily harmed or affected","example":"Economic dependence can increase a person’s vulnerability."},{"category":"Nouns","n":52,"word":"implication","vi":"hàm ý; hệ quả","simple":"a possible effect or consequence that is not always immediately obvious","example":"The widespread use of AI has major implications for education."},{"category":"Nouns","n":53,"word":"initiative","vi":"sáng kiến; sự chủ động","simple":"a new plan or action intended to solve a problem","example":"The city launched an initiative to encourage cycling."},{"category":"Nouns","n":54,"word":"gratification","vi":"sự thỏa mãn","simple":"a feeling of pleasure or satisfaction after getting what you want","example":"Social media is often designed to provide instant gratification."},{"category":"Nouns","n":55,"word":"legitimacy","vi":"tính chính đáng","simple":"the quality of being accepted as reasonable, lawful, or valid","example":"Transparent procedures can strengthen the legitimacy of public decisions."},{"category":"Nouns","n":56,"word":"prevalence","vi":"mức độ phổ biến","simple":"the fact that something is common or widespread","example":"The prevalence of smartphones has changed how people consume news."},{"category":"Nouns","n":57,"word":"productivity","vi":"năng suất","simple":"the amount of useful work produced in a given time","example":"Adequate sleep can have a noticeable effect on productivity."},{"category":"Nouns","n":58,"word":"prosperity","vi":"sự thịnh vượng","simple":"the state of being economically successful and comfortable","example":"Economic prosperity does not automatically produce greater happiness."},{"category":"Nouns","n":59,"word":"repercussion","vi":"hệ quả tiêu cực","simple":"an indirect and usually negative consequence","example":"Poor planning can have long-term repercussions for a business."},{"category":"Nouns","n":60,"word":"shortcoming","vi":"thiếu sót","simple":"a weakness or fault in a person, system, or plan","example":"One major shortcoming of online learning is the lack of face-to-face interaction."},{"category":"Nouns","n":61,"word":"stigma","vi":"sự kỳ thị","simple":"a strong negative social judgement attached to something","example":"Public discussion can help reduce the stigma surrounding unemployment."},{"category":"Nouns","n":62,"word":"threshold","vi":"ngưỡng","simple":"the point at which something begins to happen or change","example":"People have different thresholds for stress."},{"category":"Nouns","n":63,"word":"trajectory","vi":"quỹ đạo; xu hướng phát triển","simple":"the direction in which a situation develops over time","example":"A good mentor can change the trajectory of a young person’s career."},{"category":"Nouns","n":64,"word":"transparency","vi":"tính minh bạch","simple":"the quality of being open and easy to understand","example":"Greater transparency can reduce suspicion and corruption."},{"category":"Nouns","n":65,"word":"uncertainty","vi":"sự bất định","simple":"a situation in which the future or result is not known","example":"Economic uncertainty can make consumers reluctant to spend."},{"category":"Nouns","n":66,"word":"well-being","vi":"sức khỏe và hạnh phúc","simple":"the state of being healthy, comfortable, and satisfied","example":"Regular exercise improves both physical and mental well-being."},{"category":"Nouns","n":67,"word":"affordability","vi":"khả năng chi trả","simple":"the extent to which something is reasonably priced","example":"Housing affordability is a major issue in large cities."},{"category":"Nouns","n":68,"word":"accessibility","vi":"khả năng tiếp cận","simple":"the extent to which something is easy to reach, use, or obtain","example":"Online services can improve the accessibility of education."},{"category":"Nouns","n":69,"word":"dependency","vi":"sự phụ thuộc","simple":"a situation in which someone relies heavily on another person or thing","example":"Excessive financial dependency can limit personal freedom."},{"category":"Nouns","n":70,"word":"discretion","vi":"quyền tự quyết","simple":"the freedom to make a judgement or decision in a particular situation","example":"Managers need some discretion when dealing with unusual cases."},{"category":"Nouns","n":71,"word":"feasibility","vi":"tính khả thi","simple":"the degree to which a plan can realistically be carried out","example":"The feasibility of the proposal depends largely on its cost."},{"category":"Nouns","n":72,"word":"inconsistency","vi":"sự thiếu nhất quán","simple":"a lack of agreement or a pattern of changing unpredictably","example":"Inconsistency in enforcement can undermine respect for rules."},{"category":"Nouns","n":73,"word":"magnitude","vi":"quy mô; mức độ","simple":"the great size, importance, or seriousness of something","example":"Many people underestimate the magnitude of the climate challenge."},{"category":"Nouns","n":74,"word":"momentum","vi":"đà phát triển","simple":"the force that keeps a process developing once it has started","example":"Once a healthy habit gains momentum, it becomes easier to maintain."},{"category":"Nouns","n":75,"word":"notion","vi":"quan niệm; ý niệm","simple":"an idea or belief about something","example":"I disagree with the notion that success is mainly a matter of luck."},{"category":"Nouns","n":76,"word":"proficiency","vi":"sự thành thạo","simple":"a high level of skill or ability","example":"Professional proficiency in English takes years of deliberate practice."},{"category":"Nouns","n":77,"word":"rationale","vi":"cơ sở lý luận; lý do","simple":"the underlying reason for a decision or policy","example":"The rationale behind the rule is to protect public safety."},{"category":"Nouns","n":78,"word":"setback","vi":"trở ngại; thất bại tạm thời","simple":"a problem that delays progress","example":"Failing one exam is a setback, not necessarily a long-term failure."},{"category":"Nouns","n":79,"word":"viability","vi":"tính khả thi lâu dài","simple":"the ability of something to work successfully over time","example":"The long-term viability of the project depends on stable funding."},{"category":"Nouns","n":80,"word":"aptitude","vi":"năng khiếu; khả năng","simple":"a natural ability to learn or do something well","example":"Aptitude matters, but sustained practice is usually more important."},{"category":"Nouns","n":81,"word":"benchmark","vi":"chuẩn tham chiếu","simple":"a standard used for comparison","example":"International rankings are often used as a benchmark for educational performance."},{"category":"Nouns","n":82,"word":"compatibility","vi":"tính tương thích","simple":"the ability of two things or people to work well together","example":"Long-term relationships depend partly on compatibility."},{"category":"Nouns","n":83,"word":"concession","vi":"sự nhượng bộ","simple":"something you agree to give up in order to reach agreement","example":"Both sides made concessions to avoid a prolonged dispute."},{"category":"Nouns","n":84,"word":"conformity","vi":"sự tuân thủ; đồng nhất","simple":"behaviour that follows accepted social rules or expectations","example":"Excessive pressure for conformity can discourage originality."},{"category":"Nouns","n":85,"word":"deterrent","vi":"yếu tố răn đe","simple":"something that discourages an unwanted action","example":"A meaningful fine can act as a deterrent to dangerous driving."},{"category":"Nouns","n":86,"word":"drawback","vi":"nhược điểm","simple":"a disadvantage or negative feature","example":"One drawback of remote work is the lack of informal social contact."},{"category":"Nouns","n":87,"word":"entitlement","vi":"quyền lợi","simple":"a right to receive or do something","example":"Access to basic education should be treated as an entitlement rather than a privilege."},{"category":"Nouns","n":88,"word":"expertise","vi":"chuyên môn","simple":"advanced knowledge or skill in a particular area","example":"Complex decisions often require specialist expertise."},{"category":"Nouns","n":89,"word":"loophole","vi":"kẽ hở","simple":"a weakness in a rule that allows people to avoid its intended effect","example":"Companies may exploit legal loopholes unless regulations are carefully written."},{"category":"Nouns","n":90,"word":"merit","vi":"ưu điểm; giá trị","simple":"a good quality or reason that makes something worth considering","example":"The proposal has merit, but its cost remains a serious concern."},{"category":"Nouns","n":91,"word":"negligence","vi":"sự cẩu thả; tắc trách","simple":"failure to give proper care or attention","example":"Serious accidents can result from negligence rather than bad luck."},{"category":"Nouns","n":92,"word":"prerequisite","vi":"điều kiện tiên quyết","simple":"something that must exist or happen before something else is possible","example":"Basic literacy is a prerequisite for many forms of further education."},{"category":"Nouns","n":93,"word":"safeguard","vi":"biện pháp bảo vệ","simple":"a measure designed to protect against harm or abuse","example":"Strong privacy safeguards are needed when sensitive data is collected."},{"category":"Nouns","n":94,"word":"stereotype","vi":"định kiến khuôn mẫu","simple":"an oversimplified belief about a type of person or group","example":"Media representation can either reinforce or challenge stereotypes."},{"category":"Nouns","n":95,"word":"subsidy","vi":"trợ cấp","simple":"money provided by a government to reduce a cost or support an activity","example":"Public transport subsidies can make commuting more affordable."},{"category":"Nouns","n":96,"word":"surplus","vi":"thặng dư; dư thừa","simple":"an amount that is more than what is needed","example":"Some countries produce a food surplus while others face shortages."},{"category":"Nouns","n":97,"word":"tolerance","vi":"sự khoan dung; sức chịu đựng","simple":"willingness to accept differences or difficulty without reacting badly","example":"Living in a diverse society can encourage greater tolerance."},{"category":"Nouns","n":98,"word":"transition","vi":"sự chuyển đổi","simple":"the process of changing from one state or system to another","example":"The transition to renewable energy will take time and investment."},{"category":"Nouns","n":99,"word":"catalyst","vi":"chất xúc tác; động lực thúc đẩy","simple":"something that causes or speeds up major change","example":"The crisis became a catalyst for rapid reform."},{"category":"Nouns","n":100,"word":"correlation","vi":"mối tương quan","simple":"a relationship in which two things change or occur together","example":"A correlation between income and health does not by itself prove causation."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":1,"word":"accessible","vi":"dễ tiếp cận","simple":"easy to reach, use, understand, or obtain","example":"Public information should be accessible to ordinary citizens."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":2,"word":"adequate","vi":"đầy đủ; thỏa đáng","simple":"good enough for a particular purpose","example":"The city does not have adequate public transport for its population."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":3,"word":"adverse","vi":"bất lợi","simple":"harmful or unfavourable","example":"Long working hours can have adverse effects on health."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":4,"word":"ambiguous","vi":"mơ hồ","simple":"unclear because it can be understood in more than one way","example":"The instructions were too ambiguous to follow confidently."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":5,"word":"arbitrary","vi":"tùy tiện","simple":"based on personal choice rather than a clear reason or system","example":"An arbitrary rule is difficult to defend."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":6,"word":"attainable","vi":"có thể đạt được","simple":"realistically possible to achieve","example":"A high score is attainable with consistent, targeted practice."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":7,"word":"compelling","vi":"thuyết phục; hấp dẫn","simple":"very convincing or able to hold attention strongly","example":"She gave a compelling argument for investing in prevention."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":8,"word":"comprehensive","vi":"toàn diện","simple":"covering nearly all important aspects","example":"The report provides a comprehensive overview of the problem."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":9,"word":"counterproductive","vi":"phản tác dụng","simple":"having the opposite effect from the one intended","example":"Punishing every minor mistake can be counterproductive."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":10,"word":"credible","vi":"đáng tin cậy","simple":"believable and worthy of trust","example":"The claim is more credible when it is supported by reliable evidence."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":11,"word":"detrimental","vi":"có hại","simple":"causing harm or damage","example":"Chronic sleep loss is detrimental to both memory and mood."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":12,"word":"diverse","vi":"đa dạng","simple":"containing many different types or forms","example":"A diverse workforce can bring a wider range of ideas."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":13,"word":"durable","vi":"bền; lâu bền","simple":"able to remain useful or in good condition for a long time","example":"I would rather buy one durable product than replace a cheap one repeatedly."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":14,"word":"efficient","vi":"hiệu quả","simple":"producing a result with little waste of time or resources","example":"An efficient transport system can reduce commuting time."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":15,"word":"feasible","vi":"khả thi","simple":"realistically possible to do","example":"The proposal sounds attractive, but I am not sure it is financially feasible."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":16,"word":"flexible","vi":"linh hoạt","simple":"able to change easily according to circumstances","example":"A flexible schedule can help employees balance work and family life."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":17,"word":"fragile","vi":"mong manh","simple":"easily damaged, weakened, or destroyed","example":"Trust is fragile and can disappear quickly after repeated dishonesty."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":18,"word":"fundamental","vi":"căn bản; nền tảng","simple":"basic and extremely important","example":"Trust is fundamental to any close relationship."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":19,"word":"impartial","vi":"không thiên vị","simple":"fair and not favouring one side","example":"A judge is expected to remain impartial."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":20,"word":"inevitable","vi":"không thể tránh khỏi","simple":"almost impossible to avoid","example":"Some degree of technological change is inevitable."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":21,"word":"innovative","vi":"đổi mới; sáng tạo","simple":"using new and effective ideas or methods","example":"The company introduced an innovative way to reduce packaging waste."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":22,"word":"intrusive","vi":"xâm phạm; gây phiền","simple":"uncomfortably interfering with someone’s privacy or personal life","example":"Constant online tracking can feel intrusive."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":23,"word":"misleading","vi":"gây hiểu lầm","simple":"likely to make people believe something that is not fully true","example":"A single statistic can be misleading without proper context."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":24,"word":"negligible","vi":"không đáng kể","simple":"so small that it is almost unimportant","example":"The difference in price was negligible."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":25,"word":"obsolete","vi":"lỗi thời","simple":"no longer useful because something newer has replaced it","example":"Some office skills may become obsolete as technology changes."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":26,"word":"plausible","vi":"hợp lý; có vẻ đáng tin","simple":"reasonable enough to seem possible or true","example":"That is a plausible explanation, although it is difficult to prove."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":27,"word":"prevalent","vi":"phổ biến","simple":"common and widespread","example":"Remote work is increasingly prevalent in knowledge-based industries."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":28,"word":"profound","vi":"sâu sắc","simple":"very great, deep, or important","example":"Becoming a parent can have a profound effect on a person’s priorities."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":29,"word":"rational","vi":"hợp lý; lý trí","simple":"based on logic and reasonable judgement","example":"It is rational to compare long-term costs rather than just the initial price."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":30,"word":"reluctant","vi":"miễn cưỡng","simple":"not willing or eager to do something","example":"Some older workers are reluctant to adopt unfamiliar technology."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":31,"word":"resilient","vi":"kiên cường; dễ phục hồi","simple":"able to recover quickly after difficulty","example":"Children can be remarkably resilient when they receive proper support."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":32,"word":"scarce","vi":"khan hiếm","simple":"available only in small amounts","example":"Affordable housing is scarce in many capital cities."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":33,"word":"sceptical","vi":"hoài nghi","simple":"not easily convinced that something is true or useful","example":"I am sceptical of claims that promise instant results."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":34,"word":"substantial","vi":"đáng kể; lớn","simple":"large enough to be important or noticeable","example":"The policy would require substantial public investment."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":35,"word":"sustainable","vi":"bền vững","simple":"able to continue for a long time without causing serious harm","example":"Cycling is a more sustainable form of urban transport."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":36,"word":"tangible","vi":"hữu hình; rõ ràng","simple":"clear and real enough to be seen, measured, or experienced","example":"The training produced tangible improvements in staff performance."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":37,"word":"temporary","vi":"tạm thời","simple":"lasting for only a limited period","example":"Working from home was initially a temporary arrangement."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":38,"word":"vulnerable","vi":"dễ bị tổn thương","simple":"easily harmed, affected, or exploited","example":"Children are particularly vulnerable to misleading advertising."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":39,"word":"worthwhile","vi":"đáng làm; đáng giá","simple":"valuable enough to justify the time, money, or effort","example":"Learning another language is demanding but worthwhile."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":40,"word":"excessive","vi":"quá mức","simple":"more than is reasonable or necessary","example":"Excessive screen time can interfere with sleep."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":41,"word":"indispensable","vi":"không thể thiếu","simple":"so important that it is difficult to manage without it","example":"The internet has become indispensable for many businesses."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":42,"word":"inherent","vi":"vốn có","simple":"existing as a natural or permanent part of something","example":"There is an inherent risk in every investment."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":43,"word":"lucrative","vi":"sinh lợi cao","simple":"producing a large amount of money","example":"Some people choose a lucrative career even if they find it unfulfilling."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":44,"word":"marginal","vi":"rất nhỏ; không đáng kể","simple":"small and not very important","example":"The new system produced only a marginal improvement."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":45,"word":"moderate","vi":"vừa phải","simple":"not extreme in amount, degree, or intensity","example":"Moderate exercise is beneficial for most adults."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":46,"word":"pervasive","vi":"lan rộng; phổ biến","simple":"present or noticeable throughout a place or situation","example":"Advertising has become pervasive in digital life."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":47,"word":"practical","vi":"thực tế","simple":"suitable for real situations and likely to work","example":"Public policy needs to be practical as well as idealistic."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":48,"word":"rigid","vi":"cứng nhắc","simple":"not able or willing to change","example":"A rigid schedule may not suit people with family responsibilities."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":49,"word":"spontaneous","vi":"tự phát; tự nhiên","simple":"done naturally without being planned in advance","example":"Some of my best travel experiences were completely spontaneous."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":50,"word":"superficial","vi":"hời hợt","simple":"only dealing with the surface rather than the deeper issue","example":"Social media can encourage superficial judgements about other people."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":51,"word":"transparent","vi":"minh bạch","simple":"open, clear, and easy to understand","example":"A transparent hiring process is more likely to be trusted."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":52,"word":"unpredictable","vi":"khó lường","simple":"difficult or impossible to know in advance","example":"The weather has become increasingly unpredictable."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":53,"word":"unprecedented","vi":"chưa từng có","simple":"never having happened or existed before","example":"The pandemic created unprecedented disruption to international travel."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":54,"word":"viable","vi":"khả thi; có thể tồn tại","simple":"capable of working successfully over time","example":"Public transport is only a viable alternative if it is reliable and affordable."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":55,"word":"widespread","vi":"phổ biến rộng rãi","simple":"existing or happening in many places or among many people","example":"There is widespread concern about online misinformation."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":56,"word":"coherent","vi":"mạch lạc","simple":"logical, connected, and easy to follow","example":"A strong answer needs a coherent line of reasoning."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":57,"word":"concise","vi":"súc tích","simple":"clear and complete without unnecessary words","example":"Her explanation was concise but informative."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":58,"word":"controversial","vi":"gây tranh cãi","simple":"causing strong disagreement","example":"Facial recognition remains a controversial technology."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":59,"word":"cumulative","vi":"tích lũy","simple":"increasing gradually as more is added over time","example":"The cumulative effect of small habits can be significant."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":60,"word":"disproportionate","vi":"không cân xứng","simple":"too large or too small in relation to something else","example":"Low-income households often bear a disproportionate share of rising energy costs."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":61,"word":"ethical","vi":"có đạo đức","simple":"morally acceptable and responsible","example":"Companies should consider whether their use of personal data is ethical."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":62,"word":"flawed","vi":"có khuyết điểm","simple":"containing an important weakness or mistake","example":"The argument is appealing, but its basic assumption is flawed."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":63,"word":"holistic","vi":"toàn diện","simple":"considering the whole situation rather than one part","example":"A holistic approach to health includes sleep, diet, exercise, and stress management."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":64,"word":"inclusive","vi":"bao trùm; hòa nhập","simple":"designed to include people with different needs or backgrounds","example":"Schools should create a more inclusive learning environment."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":65,"word":"inconsistent","vi":"thiếu nhất quán","simple":"not staying the same or not agreeing with itself","example":"Inconsistent enforcement makes rules less effective."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":66,"word":"insufficient","vi":"không đủ","simple":"not enough for a particular purpose","example":"Short-term funding is insufficient for a long-term infrastructure project."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":67,"word":"legitimate","vi":"chính đáng; hợp pháp","simple":"reasonable, acceptable, or lawful","example":"Privacy is a legitimate concern when governments collect personal data."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":68,"word":"meaningful","vi":"có ý nghĩa","simple":"important enough to have a real effect or value","example":"Small changes can still produce meaningful improvements."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":69,"word":"nuanced","vi":"tinh tế; đa sắc thái","simple":"showing subtle differences rather than a simple yes-or-no view","example":"The issue requires a more nuanced discussion."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":70,"word":"objective","vi":"khách quan","simple":"based on facts rather than personal feelings","example":"It is difficult to remain completely objective when judging your own performance."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":71,"word":"overwhelming","vi":"áp đảo; quá sức","simple":"so great that it is difficult to deal with","example":"The amount of information online can be overwhelming."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":72,"word":"persistent","vi":"dai dẳng; kiên trì","simple":"continuing for a long time despite attempts to stop it","example":"Persistent inequality can damage social trust."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":73,"word":"precise","vi":"chính xác","simple":"exact and accurate","example":"Using precise language makes an argument easier to understand."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":74,"word":"receptive","vi":"cởi mở; dễ tiếp thu","simple":"willing to consider new ideas or suggestions","example":"Young children are often highly receptive to new languages."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":75,"word":"redundant","vi":"dư thừa; không cần thiết","simple":"no longer needed or useful","example":"Some repetitive administrative tasks may become redundant."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":76,"word":"relevant","vi":"có liên quan","simple":"directly connected to the issue being discussed","example":"Examples should be relevant to the main argument."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":77,"word":"robust","vi":"vững chắc","simple":"strong and able to work well under difficult conditions","example":"A robust system should continue functioning even when demand suddenly increases."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":78,"word":"subtle","vi":"tinh tế; khó nhận thấy","simple":"not obvious and requiring careful attention to notice","example":"Tone can communicate subtle differences in attitude."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":79,"word":"tentative","vi":"tạm thời; chưa chắc chắn","simple":"not fully certain or decided","example":"We reached a tentative agreement but still had several details to discuss."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":80,"word":"unrealistic","vi":"không thực tế","simple":"not based on what is likely or practically possible","example":"Expecting perfect results immediately is unrealistic."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":81,"word":"volatile","vi":"biến động mạnh","simple":"likely to change suddenly and unpredictably","example":"Cryptocurrency prices can be extremely volatile."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":82,"word":"compulsory","vi":"bắt buộc","simple":"required by a rule or law","example":"In many countries, education is compulsory until a certain age."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":83,"word":"adaptable","vi":"dễ thích nghi","simple":"able to change successfully when circumstances change","example":"Adaptable workers are better prepared for rapid technological change."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":84,"word":"affluent","vi":"giàu có","simple":"having a relatively high level of wealth","example":"Affluent households can usually absorb price increases more easily."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":85,"word":"autonomous","vi":"tự chủ","simple":"able to make decisions independently","example":"Autonomous learners take responsibility for their own progress."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":86,"word":"compatible","vi":"tương thích","simple":"able to exist or work together without serious conflict","example":"Economic growth is not always compatible with unlimited resource consumption."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":87,"word":"conventional","vi":"truyền thống; thông thường","simple":"following traditional or widely accepted methods or ideas","example":"Conventional classroom teaching still has advantages in some situations."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":88,"word":"equitable","vi":"công bằng","simple":"fair in a way that takes different needs into account","example":"A tax system should be both efficient and equitable."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":89,"word":"explicit","vi":"rõ ràng; minh thị","simple":"stated clearly and directly","example":"The policy needs explicit rules about how personal data may be used."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":90,"word":"intuitive","vi":"trực quan; dễ hiểu","simple":"easy to understand or use without much explanation","example":"A well-designed app should feel intuitive to new users."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":91,"word":"mandatory","vi":"bắt buộc","simple":"required by a rule or law","example":"Safety training is mandatory for all new employees."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":92,"word":"mediocre","vi":"tầm thường","simple":"only average and not especially good","example":"A high price does not prevent a product from being mediocre."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":93,"word":"selective","vi":"có chọn lọc","simple":"careful about choosing only certain people or things","example":"People are often selective about the information they believe online."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":94,"word":"stable","vi":"ổn định","simple":"unlikely to change suddenly or unpredictably","example":"A stable income makes long-term financial planning easier."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":95,"word":"stagnant","vi":"trì trệ","simple":"not growing, developing, or changing","example":"Wages may remain stagnant even when living costs rise."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":96,"word":"stringent","vi":"nghiêm ngặt","simple":"very strict and demanding","example":"Stringent safety standards can reduce preventable accidents."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":97,"word":"versatile","vi":"đa năng","simple":"able to be used effectively in many different ways","example":"English is a versatile skill that can support many different careers."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":98,"word":"incremental","vi":"từng bước; tăng dần","simple":"happening through a series of small changes","example":"Incremental improvements can produce substantial results over time."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":99,"word":"interchangeable","vi":"có thể thay thế lẫn nhau","simple":"similar enough to be used in place of each other","example":"These two terms are related, but they are not completely interchangeable."},{"category":"Adjectives","n":100,"word":"proportionate","vi":"tương xứng","simple":"appropriate in size or degree compared with the situation","example":"Any restriction should be proportionate to the actual level of risk."},{"category":"Verbs","n":1,"word":"acknowledge","vi":"thừa nhận","simple":"accept or recognise that something is true or important","example":"We should acknowledge that every policy has limitations."},{"category":"Verbs","n":2,"word":"adapt","vi":"thích nghi","simple":"change your behaviour or methods to suit a new situation","example":"Workers need to adapt as technology changes."},{"category":"Verbs","n":3,"word":"advocate","vi":"ủng hộ; chủ trương","simple":"publicly support an idea, policy, or action","example":"Some experts advocate stricter controls on targeted advertising."},{"category":"Verbs","n":4,"word":"allocate","vi":"phân bổ","simple":"decide how money, time, or resources should be distributed","example":"Governments must allocate limited resources carefully."},{"category":"Verbs","n":5,"word":"anticipate","vi":"dự đoán; lường trước","simple":"expect something and prepare for it before it happens","example":"Good managers anticipate problems rather than merely reacting to them."},{"category":"Verbs","n":6,"word":"assess","vi":"đánh giá","simple":"judge the quality, importance, or likely effect of something","example":"It is difficult to assess the long-term impact of the policy."},{"category":"Verbs","n":7,"word":"attain","vi":"đạt được","simple":"successfully reach a goal or level","example":"Fluency takes time to attain."},{"category":"Verbs","n":8,"word":"bolster","vi":"củng cố; thúc đẩy","simple":"make something stronger or more effective","example":"Better training could bolster public confidence in the service."},{"category":"Verbs","n":9,"word":"clarify","vi":"làm rõ","simple":"make an idea or situation easier to understand","example":"The government should clarify how the new rule will be enforced."},{"category":"Verbs","n":10,"word":"collaborate","vi":"hợp tác","simple":"work together to achieve a shared goal","example":"Universities and businesses can collaborate on research projects."},{"category":"Verbs","n":11,"word":"compensate","vi":"bù đắp","simple":"provide something that balances a loss or disadvantage","example":"Higher salaries may compensate for longer working hours."},{"category":"Verbs","n":12,"word":"compromise","vi":"thỏa hiệp","simple":"accept less than you originally wanted in order to reach agreement","example":"Both sides may need to compromise."},{"category":"Verbs","n":13,"word":"constrain","vi":"hạn chế","simple":"limit what someone can do","example":"High costs can constrain access to higher education."},{"category":"Verbs","n":14,"word":"contribute","vi":"đóng góp","simple":"help cause or improve a particular result","example":"Lack of sleep can contribute to poor concentration."},{"category":"Verbs","n":15,"word":"convey","vi":"truyền đạt","simple":"communicate an idea, feeling, or meaning","example":"Body language can convey confidence even before a person speaks."},{"category":"Verbs","n":16,"word":"cope","vi":"đối phó; xoay xở","simple":"manage successfully in a difficult situation","example":"People need effective ways to cope with stress."},{"category":"Verbs","n":17,"word":"curb","vi":"kiềm chế","simple":"reduce or control something undesirable","example":"Higher taxes may help curb excessive consumption."},{"category":"Verbs","n":18,"word":"deteriorate","vi":"xấu đi; suy giảm","simple":"become progressively worse","example":"Without maintenance, public infrastructure can deteriorate quickly."},{"category":"Verbs","n":19,"word":"diminish","vi":"làm giảm; suy giảm","simple":"make or become smaller, weaker, or less important","example":"Constant interruptions can diminish productivity."},{"category":"Verbs","n":20,"word":"discourage","vi":"làm nản lòng; ngăn cản","simple":"make someone less willing to do something","example":"Complex procedures may discourage people from applying."},{"category":"Verbs","n":21,"word":"distort","vi":"bóp méo","simple":"make something appear different from the truth","example":"Social media can distort people’s perception of normal life."},{"category":"Verbs","n":22,"word":"diversify","vi":"đa dạng hóa","simple":"increase the range of activities, products, or options","example":"Workers can diversify their skills to reduce career risk."},{"category":"Verbs","n":23,"word":"eliminate","vi":"loại bỏ","simple":"remove something completely","example":"Technology can eliminate some repetitive tasks."},{"category":"Verbs","n":24,"word":"emerge","vi":"xuất hiện","simple":"appear or become known","example":"New problems often emerge when a system grows rapidly."},{"category":"Verbs","n":25,"word":"enhance","vi":"nâng cao","simple":"improve the quality or value of something","example":"Regular feedback can enhance learning."},{"category":"Verbs","n":26,"word":"exacerbate","vi":"làm trầm trọng hơn","simple":"make an existing problem more serious","example":"Poor planning can exacerbate traffic congestion."},{"category":"Verbs","n":27,"word":"facilitate","vi":"tạo điều kiện","simple":"make a process easier or more likely to happen","example":"Technology can facilitate communication across long distances."},{"category":"Verbs","n":28,"word":"foster","vi":"thúc đẩy; nuôi dưỡng","simple":"encourage the development of something positive","example":"Team projects can foster cooperation."},{"category":"Verbs","n":29,"word":"hinder","vi":"cản trở","simple":"make progress more difficult","example":"Fear of making mistakes can hinder language development."},{"category":"Verbs","n":30,"word":"illustrate","vi":"minh họa","simple":"show an idea clearly by giving an example","example":"This example illustrates why flexibility matters."},{"category":"Verbs","n":31,"word":"implement","vi":"triển khai; thực hiện","simple":"put a plan, rule, or system into action","example":"A policy is useless if it is not implemented properly."},{"category":"Verbs","n":32,"word":"imply","vi":"hàm ý","simple":"suggest something without stating it directly","example":"A high salary does not necessarily imply high job satisfaction."},{"category":"Verbs","n":33,"word":"impose","vi":"áp đặt","simple":"force a rule, cost, or restriction on someone","example":"The city imposed stricter parking restrictions."},{"category":"Verbs","n":34,"word":"incentivise","vi":"tạo động lực; khuyến khích","simple":"give people a reason or reward to encourage an action","example":"Tax benefits can incentivise companies to reduce emissions."},{"category":"Verbs","n":35,"word":"justify","vi":"biện minh; lý giải","simple":"show that something is reasonable or necessary","example":"The potential benefits do not justify excessive surveillance."},{"category":"Verbs","n":36,"word":"maintain","vi":"duy trì","simple":"keep something at the same level or condition","example":"It can be difficult to maintain motivation over several years."},{"category":"Verbs","n":37,"word":"mitigate","vi":"giảm nhẹ","simple":"reduce the seriousness or harmful effect of something","example":"Better drainage can mitigate the impact of flooding."},{"category":"Verbs","n":38,"word":"outweigh","vi":"quan trọng hơn; vượt trội hơn","simple":"be more important or greater than something else","example":"For me, the benefits of living alone outweigh the disadvantages."},{"category":"Verbs","n":39,"word":"perceive","vi":"nhận thức","simple":"see, understand, or think about something in a particular way","example":"People may perceive the same situation very differently."},{"category":"Verbs","n":40,"word":"prioritise","vi":"ưu tiên","simple":"decide which things are most important and deal with them first","example":"Students need to prioritise tasks when deadlines overlap."},{"category":"Verbs","n":41,"word":"regulate","vi":"điều tiết; quản lý","simple":"control an activity through rules or laws","example":"Governments increasingly regulate how companies handle personal data."},{"category":"Verbs","n":42,"word":"reinforce","vi":"củng cố","simple":"make an idea, habit, or structure stronger","example":"Repeated success can reinforce confidence."},{"category":"Verbs","n":43,"word":"retain","vi":"giữ lại; duy trì","simple":"continue to have, keep, or remember something","example":"People retain information better when they use it actively."},{"category":"Verbs","n":44,"word":"scrutinise","vi":"xem xét kỹ","simple":"examine something very carefully","example":"Consumers should scrutinise claims that sound too good to be true."},{"category":"Verbs","n":45,"word":"stimulate","vi":"kích thích; thúc đẩy","simple":"encourage activity, growth, or interest","example":"Investment in infrastructure can stimulate economic activity."},{"category":"Verbs","n":46,"word":"undermine","vi":"làm suy yếu","simple":"gradually weaken something","example":"Repeated dishonesty can undermine trust."},{"category":"Verbs","n":47,"word":"alleviate","vi":"làm giảm; xoa dịu","simple":"make pain or a difficult situation less severe","example":"Flexible hours can alleviate pressure on working parents."},{"category":"Verbs","n":48,"word":"broaden","vi":"mở rộng","simple":"make something wider or more varied","example":"Travel can broaden a person’s perspective."},{"category":"Verbs","n":49,"word":"cultivate","vi":"nuôi dưỡng; phát triển","simple":"develop a quality, habit, or skill over time","example":"Reading widely helps cultivate critical thinking."},{"category":"Verbs","n":50,"word":"derive","vi":"thu được; suy ra","simple":"obtain something from a particular source","example":"Many people derive a sense of identity from their work."},{"category":"Verbs","n":51,"word":"deviate","vi":"lệch khỏi","simple":"move away from a plan, standard, or usual pattern","example":"It is sometimes necessary to deviate from the original plan."},{"category":"Verbs","n":52,"word":"disrupt","vi":"làm gián đoạn","simple":"interrupt the normal operation of something","example":"A transport strike can disrupt an entire city."},{"category":"Verbs","n":53,"word":"embrace","vi":"đón nhận","simple":"accept and willingly adopt a new idea or change","example":"Some companies have embraced remote work."},{"category":"Verbs","n":54,"word":"encounter","vi":"gặp phải","simple":"experience or meet a problem or situation unexpectedly","example":"International students often encounter cultural differences."},{"category":"Verbs","n":55,"word":"evaluate","vi":"đánh giá","simple":"judge something carefully using evidence or criteria","example":"We should evaluate the policy after enough data has been collected."},{"category":"Verbs","n":56,"word":"exploit","vi":"khai thác","simple":"use an opportunity or resource for advantage, sometimes unfairly","example":"Some platforms exploit users’ attention to maximise advertising revenue."},{"category":"Verbs","n":57,"word":"generate","vi":"tạo ra","simple":"produce or create something","example":"Tourism can generate employment in rural areas."},{"category":"Verbs","n":58,"word":"inhibit","vi":"kìm hãm","simple":"prevent or slow down an action or process","example":"Fear can inhibit creativity."},{"category":"Verbs","n":59,"word":"integrate","vi":"tích hợp","simple":"combine parts so they work together effectively","example":"Schools should integrate digital tools into lessons carefully."},{"category":"Verbs","n":60,"word":"interpret","vi":"diễn giải","simple":"decide what information or behaviour means","example":"People interpret statistics differently depending on context."},{"category":"Verbs","n":61,"word":"intervene","vi":"can thiệp","simple":"become involved in order to change an outcome","example":"Authorities may need to intervene when public safety is at risk."},{"category":"Verbs","n":62,"word":"neglect","vi":"bỏ bê; lơ là","simple":"fail to give enough attention or care to something","example":"People sometimes neglect their health when work becomes demanding."},{"category":"Verbs","n":63,"word":"offset","vi":"bù đắp","simple":"balance a negative effect with a positive one","example":"Higher productivity may offset some of the additional costs."},{"category":"Verbs","n":64,"word":"preserve","vi":"bảo tồn; gìn giữ","simple":"protect something so it continues to exist","example":"Cities should preserve historic buildings where possible."},{"category":"Verbs","n":65,"word":"promote","vi":"thúc đẩy","simple":"encourage or support the development of something","example":"Public campaigns can promote healthier eating habits."},{"category":"Verbs","n":66,"word":"prompt","vi":"thúc đẩy; khiến","simple":"cause someone to think or act","example":"The incident prompted the company to review its safety procedures."},{"category":"Verbs","n":67,"word":"pursue","vi":"theo đuổi","simple":"continue trying to achieve a goal","example":"Many graduates pursue further study to improve their career prospects."},{"category":"Verbs","n":68,"word":"recover","vi":"phục hồi","simple":"return to a normal or better condition after difficulty","example":"Small businesses may take years to recover from a major economic shock."},{"category":"Verbs","n":69,"word":"rectify","vi":"khắc phục; sửa chữa","simple":"correct a problem or mistake","example":"The company acted quickly to rectify the error."},{"category":"Verbs","n":70,"word":"refine","vi":"tinh chỉnh","simple":"improve something by making small changes","example":"Practice helps learners refine their pronunciation."},{"category":"Verbs","n":71,"word":"restrict","vi":"hạn chế","simple":"limit what someone can do or access","example":"Some countries restrict advertising aimed at children."},{"category":"Verbs","n":72,"word":"sustain","vi":"duy trì","simple":"keep something continuing over time","example":"It is difficult to sustain rapid growth indefinitely."},{"category":"Verbs","n":73,"word":"tackle","vi":"giải quyết","simple":"make a serious effort to deal with a problem","example":"Governments need to tackle the causes of housing shortages."},{"category":"Verbs","n":74,"word":"trigger","vi":"kích hoạt; gây ra","simple":"cause an event or reaction to begin","example":"A sudden rise in prices can trigger public concern."},{"category":"Verbs","n":75,"word":"validate","vi":"xác nhận; chứng minh","simple":"confirm that an idea, feeling, or result is reasonable or accurate","example":"Further research is needed to validate the findings."},{"category":"Verbs","n":76,"word":"withstand","vi":"chống chịu","simple":"remain strong despite pressure or difficulty","example":"Good infrastructure should withstand extreme weather."},{"category":"Verbs","n":77,"word":"accommodate","vi":"đáp ứng; thích ứng","simple":"adjust to provide enough space or meet different needs","example":"Workplaces should accommodate employees with different family responsibilities."},{"category":"Verbs","n":78,"word":"accumulate","vi":"tích lũy","simple":"gradually collect or increase over time","example":"Small debts can accumulate surprisingly quickly."},{"category":"Verbs","n":79,"word":"articulate","vi":"diễn đạt rõ ràng","simple":"express an idea clearly and effectively","example":"Candidates need to articulate their opinions rather than list memorised phrases."},{"category":"Verbs","n":80,"word":"attribute","vi":"quy cho","simple":"regard something as being caused by a particular factor","example":"Some people attribute their success mainly to discipline."},{"category":"Verbs","n":81,"word":"avert","vi":"ngăn chặn","simple":"prevent something bad from happening","example":"Early action may avert a more serious crisis."},{"category":"Verbs","n":82,"word":"consolidate","vi":"củng cố; hợp nhất","simple":"make something stronger or more secure after progress has been made","example":"Regular revision helps consolidate new vocabulary."},{"category":"Verbs","n":83,"word":"contemplate","vi":"cân nhắc","simple":"think carefully about a possible action or future event","example":"Many people contemplate changing careers at some point."},{"category":"Verbs","n":84,"word":"contradict","vi":"mâu thuẫn; phản bác","simple":"say or show the opposite of another statement or idea","example":"The new evidence appears to contradict the original claim."},{"category":"Verbs","n":85,"word":"coordinate","vi":"phối hợp","simple":"organise people or activities so they work together effectively","example":"Large projects require several departments to coordinate closely."},{"category":"Verbs","n":86,"word":"disclose","vi":"tiết lộ","simple":"make information known, especially information that was private","example":"Companies should disclose how customer data is used."},{"category":"Verbs","n":87,"word":"distinguish","vi":"phân biệt","simple":"recognise or explain the difference between two things","example":"Children gradually learn to distinguish advertising from ordinary content."},{"category":"Verbs","n":88,"word":"dominate","vi":"chi phối","simple":"be much more powerful, important, or noticeable than others","example":"A few large companies dominate the market."},{"category":"Verbs","n":89,"word":"endure","vi":"chịu đựng; kéo dài","simple":"continue through a difficult or unpleasant situation","example":"People may endure short-term inconvenience for a long-term benefit."},{"category":"Verbs","n":90,"word":"establish","vi":"thiết lập","simple":"create or prove something clearly","example":"The study does not establish a direct causal relationship."},{"category":"Verbs","n":91,"word":"exceed","vi":"vượt quá","simple":"be greater than a particular amount or level","example":"Demand can exceed supply in rapidly growing cities."},{"category":"Verbs","n":92,"word":"expose","vi":"phơi bày; làm tiếp xúc","simple":"make someone experience or become aware of something","example":"Travel exposes people to unfamiliar customs and viewpoints."},{"category":"Verbs","n":93,"word":"fluctuate","vi":"dao động","simple":"rise and fall irregularly","example":"Energy prices can fluctuate considerably."},{"category":"Verbs","n":94,"word":"formulate","vi":"xây dựng; đề ra","simple":"develop an idea, plan, or argument carefully","example":"Students should formulate a clear position before they begin writing."},{"category":"Verbs","n":95,"word":"infer","vi":"suy luận","simple":"reach a conclusion from evidence rather than a direct statement","example":"We cannot infer causation from a simple correlation."},{"category":"Verbs","n":96,"word":"navigate","vi":"xoay xở; định hướng","simple":"deal successfully with a complex situation or system","example":"Young adults often need help navigating the job market."},{"category":"Verbs","n":97,"word":"overlook","vi":"bỏ qua","simple":"fail to notice or consider something important","example":"Policy makers sometimes overlook the needs of rural communities."},{"category":"Verbs","n":98,"word":"resolve","vi":"giải quyết","simple":"find a satisfactory solution to a problem","example":"Open communication can resolve many workplace conflicts."},{"category":"Verbs","n":99,"word":"transform","vi":"biến đổi","simple":"change something greatly in form, appearance, or function","example":"Digital technology has transformed the way people access information."},{"category":"Verbs","n":100,"word":"verify","vi":"xác minh","simple":"check that something is accurate or true","example":"People should verify information before sharing it online."}],"vocabProtocol":["Round 1 - Recognition: read the advanced word and explain it aloud using the simple paraphrase.","Round 2 - Retrieval: cover the word, read only the paraphrase, and recover the advanced word.","Round 3 - Flexibility: create a new sentence about your own life or a common IELTS topic.","Round 4 - Rescue mode: deliberately ban the advanced word and explain the same idea naturally in simple English.","Round 5 - Spaced review: revisit difficult items after 1 day, 3 days, 7 days, and 14 days."],"logic":[{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":1,"advanced":"X exacerbates Y.","simple":"X makes Y worse.","alternative":"X adds to the problem and makes it more serious."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":2,"advanced":"X contributes to Y.","simple":"X is one of the things that causes Y.","alternative":"X plays a part in creating Y."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":3,"advanced":"X stems from Y.","simple":"X happens mainly because of Y.","alternative":"Y is one of the main reasons X happens."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":4,"advanced":"X can be attributed to Y.","simple":"Y is probably one of the reasons for X.","alternative":"X may happen because of Y."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":5,"advanced":"X gives rise to Y.","simple":"X causes Y to appear or develop.","alternative":"Y can develop as a result of X."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":6,"advanced":"X triggers Y.","simple":"X causes Y to start suddenly.","alternative":"Y begins because of X."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":7,"advanced":"X has far-reaching consequences for Y.","simple":"X can affect Y in many important ways over a long period.","alternative":"The effects of X on Y can be serious and long-lasting."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":8,"advanced":"X has a knock-on effect on Y.","simple":"X causes another effect that then affects Y.","alternative":"One effect of X leads to further changes in Y."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":9,"advanced":"X undermines Y.","simple":"X gradually makes Y weaker.","alternative":"Because of X, Y becomes less effective or less stable."},{"category":"Cause and Effect","n":10,"advanced":"X reinforces Y.","simple":"X makes Y stronger or more likely to continue.","alternative":"X strengthens the existing pattern of Y."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":11,"advanced":"The benefits of X outweigh the drawbacks.","simple":"The good sides of X are more important than the bad sides.","alternative":"Overall, X gives more advantages than disadvantages."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":12,"advanced":"X comes at the expense of Y.","simple":"You gain X, but you lose or weaken Y.","alternative":"Getting X often means sacrificing Y."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":13,"advanced":"There is a trade-off between X and Y.","simple":"Improving X usually means giving up some Y.","alternative":"It is difficult to maximise both X and Y at the same time."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":14,"advanced":"X offers diminishing returns.","simple":"After a certain point, more X gives less extra benefit.","alternative":"The first increases in X help a lot, but later increases help much less."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":15,"advanced":"X yields tangible benefits.","simple":"X produces clear and noticeable advantages.","alternative":"The positive results of X can actually be seen or measured."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":16,"advanced":"X imposes a substantial burden on Y.","simple":"X creates a serious cost or difficulty for Y.","alternative":"Y has to deal with a lot of extra pressure because of X."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":17,"advanced":"X is a worthwhile investment.","simple":"X is worth the time, money, or effort it requires.","alternative":"The long-term benefit of X justifies the cost."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":18,"advanced":"X is economically viable.","simple":"X can realistically work and survive financially.","alternative":"X can probably pay for itself or operate successfully over time."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":19,"advanced":"X is financially prohibitive.","simple":"X is too expensive for many people to afford.","alternative":"The cost of X makes it unrealistic for many people."},{"category":"Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","n":20,"advanced":"X provides only marginal gains.","simple":"X improves the situation only a little.","alternative":"The benefit from X is quite small."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":21,"advanced":"X pales in comparison with Y.","simple":"X seems much less important or impressive than Y.","alternative":"Compared with Y, X is relatively minor."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":22,"advanced":"X is broadly comparable to Y.","simple":"X and Y are similar in the main ways that matter.","alternative":"There is no major difference between X and Y overall."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":23,"advanced":"X differs fundamentally from Y.","simple":"X and Y are different at a basic level.","alternative":"The main idea behind X is very different from Y."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":24,"advanced":"The distinction between X and Y is often blurred.","simple":"It is often difficult to tell exactly where X ends and Y begins.","alternative":"In real life, X and Y are not always clearly separate."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":25,"advanced":"X is disproportionately affected by Y.","simple":"Y affects X more strongly than it affects others.","alternative":"X carries an unusually large share of the impact of Y."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":26,"advanced":"X is more pronounced in Y.","simple":"X is stronger or easier to notice in Y.","alternative":"You can see X more clearly in Y."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":27,"advanced":"X and Y are not mutually exclusive.","simple":"It is possible to have both X and Y.","alternative":"Choosing X does not necessarily mean giving up Y."},{"category":"Comparison and Contrast","n":28,"advanced":"X is the lesser of two evils.","simple":"Both choices are bad, but X is less harmful.","alternative":"X is not ideal, but it is better than the alternative."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":29,"advanced":"I am inclined to believe that X.","simple":"I tend to think X is true.","alternative":"My view is generally that X."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":30,"advanced":"I remain unconvinced that X.","simple":"I still do not fully believe X.","alternative":"I do not think the evidence for X is strong enough."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":31,"advanced":"There is a compelling case for X.","simple":"There are very strong reasons to support X.","alternative":"The arguments in favour of X are convincing."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":32,"advanced":"X is difficult to justify.","simple":"There are not many good reasons to defend X.","alternative":"I do not think X can easily be defended."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":33,"advanced":"X is a legitimate concern.","simple":"It is reasonable for people to worry about X.","alternative":"Concern about X is understandable and valid."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":34,"advanced":"X is often overstated.","simple":"People often make X sound more serious or important than it really is.","alternative":"The importance of X is sometimes exaggerated."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":35,"advanced":"X should not be dismissed outright.","simple":"We should not reject X without considering it carefully.","alternative":"X may still have value and deserves proper consideration."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":36,"advanced":"A more nuanced view is required.","simple":"The issue is more complicated than a simple yes-or-no answer.","alternative":"We need to consider the differences and exceptions instead of oversimplifying it."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":37,"advanced":"X is a flawed assumption.","simple":"X is based on an important mistake in thinking.","alternative":"There is a problem with the basic idea behind X."},{"category":"Opinion and Evaluation","n":38,"advanced":"X is largely a matter of perspective.","simple":"Whether X seems good or bad depends on how you look at it.","alternative":"Different people can reasonably see X in different ways."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":39,"advanced":"X is highly plausible.","simple":"X seems very possible and reasonable.","alternative":"There are good reasons to think X may be true."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":40,"advanced":"The evidence for X is inconclusive.","simple":"The evidence does not clearly prove or disprove X.","alternative":"We still cannot be certain about X from the evidence available."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":41,"advanced":"X cannot be ruled out.","simple":"X is still possible.","alternative":"We do not have enough evidence to say X is impossible."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":42,"advanced":"X appears to be an isolated case.","simple":"X seems unusual rather than part of a wider pattern.","alternative":"There is little evidence that X happens frequently."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":43,"advanced":"There is little basis for assuming X.","simple":"We do not have enough reason or evidence to assume X.","alternative":"The assumption that X is true is weak."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":44,"advanced":"X is likely to persist.","simple":"X will probably continue for some time.","alternative":"There is a good chance X will not disappear soon."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":45,"advanced":"X is by no means inevitable.","simple":"X is not certain to happen.","alternative":"There are realistic ways in which X might be avoided."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":46,"advanced":"X remains an open question.","simple":"We still do not know the answer to X.","alternative":"X has not been settled yet."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":47,"advanced":"X should be interpreted with caution.","simple":"We should be careful about what conclusions we draw from X.","alternative":"X may not mean as much as it first appears to mean."},{"category":"Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","n":48,"advanced":"Correlation does not establish causation.","simple":"Two things happening together does not prove that one causes the other.","alternative":"Just because X and Y are linked does not mean X causes Y."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":49,"advanced":"X has undergone a profound transformation.","simple":"X has changed dramatically.","alternative":"X is now very different from what it used to be."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":50,"advanced":"X is gaining momentum.","simple":"X is becoming stronger or more popular as time goes on.","alternative":"More people are adopting X, so the trend is growing faster."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":51,"advanced":"X is gradually becoming obsolete.","simple":"X is slowly becoming unnecessary because newer alternatives exist.","alternative":"People are using X less because something newer has replaced it."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":52,"advanced":"X has reached a plateau.","simple":"X stopped increasing after a period of growth.","alternative":"X is no longer improving or growing very much."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":53,"advanced":"X fluctuates considerably.","simple":"X goes up and down a lot.","alternative":"The level of X changes frequently and unpredictably."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":54,"advanced":"X has become increasingly prevalent.","simple":"X is becoming more and more common.","alternative":"You can see X in more places and among more people than before."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":55,"advanced":"X is undergoing a gradual decline.","simple":"X is slowly becoming less common, strong, or successful.","alternative":"X is decreasing over time rather than falling suddenly."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":56,"advanced":"X marks a significant shift in Y.","simple":"X shows that Y is changing in an important way.","alternative":"X represents a major change in how Y works or is viewed."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":57,"advanced":"X is likely to reshape Y.","simple":"X will probably change the way Y develops or operates.","alternative":"Y may look very different in the future because of X."},{"category":"Change and Trends","n":58,"advanced":"X is accelerating.","simple":"X is happening faster than before.","alternative":"The rate of change in X is increasing."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":59,"advanced":"X addresses the root cause of Y.","simple":"X deals with the main reason Y happens.","alternative":"Instead of treating the symptoms, X targets the real source of Y."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":60,"advanced":"X merely treats the symptoms of Y.","simple":"X deals with the visible problem but not its main cause.","alternative":"X may help temporarily without solving why Y happens."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":61,"advanced":"A one-size-fits-all approach is unlikely to work.","simple":"The same solution will not suit everyone or every situation.","alternative":"Different groups probably need different solutions."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":62,"advanced":"X requires a multi-faceted approach.","simple":"X needs several different solutions working together.","alternative":"One single measure is unlikely to solve X."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":63,"advanced":"X can be mitigated rather than eliminated.","simple":"We may be able to reduce X even if we cannot remove it completely.","alternative":"The realistic goal is to make X less serious, not make it disappear."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":64,"advanced":"Preventive measures are more cost-effective than remedial action.","simple":"Preventing the problem is usually cheaper than fixing it later.","alternative":"It often costs less to stop a problem early than to repair the damage afterward."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":65,"advanced":"X creates unintended consequences.","simple":"X causes results that were not planned or expected.","alternative":"Even if X solves one problem, it may create another."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":66,"advanced":"X is difficult to implement consistently.","simple":"It is hard to make X work the same way in every situation.","alternative":"X may work well in one context but fail to work the same way in another."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":67,"advanced":"X is a short-term fix rather than a lasting solution.","simple":"X may help now but will not solve the problem for long.","alternative":"X deals with the immediate issue without creating a permanent solution."},{"category":"Problems and Solutions","n":68,"advanced":"The effectiveness of X depends on how it is implemented.","simple":"X can work well or badly depending on how people put it into practice.","alternative":"The idea itself is not enough; execution determines the result."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":69,"advanced":"People are prone to X.","simple":"People naturally tend to do or experience X.","alternative":"X is a common human tendency."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":70,"advanced":"People have a tendency to underestimate X.","simple":"People often think X is smaller or less important than it really is.","alternative":"Most people do not fully realise how significant X can be."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":71,"advanced":"X shapes people’s perception of Y.","simple":"X affects how people see or understand Y.","alternative":"Because of X, people may view Y differently."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":72,"advanced":"X creates a false sense of security.","simple":"X makes people feel safe even when the risk still exists.","alternative":"People may become less careful because X makes them think they are protected."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":73,"advanced":"X can erode self-confidence.","simple":"X can gradually make people believe in themselves less.","alternative":"Over time, X may make a person less confident."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":74,"advanced":"X fosters a sense of belonging.","simple":"X helps people feel accepted as part of a group.","alternative":"Because of X, people feel more connected to others."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":75,"advanced":"People become desensitised to X.","simple":"After repeated exposure, people react less strongly to X.","alternative":"When people see X again and again, it stops affecting them as much."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":76,"advanced":"X encourages instant gratification.","simple":"X encourages people to seek immediate pleasure instead of waiting for a bigger future benefit.","alternative":"X makes people want a reward now rather than later."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":77,"advanced":"X reinforces existing biases.","simple":"X makes beliefs or prejudices people already have even stronger.","alternative":"Instead of challenging people’s assumptions, X can strengthen them."},{"category":"People, Behaviour and Psychology","n":78,"advanced":"X requires considerable self-discipline.","simple":"X is difficult unless a person can control their habits and behaviour consistently.","alternative":"To do X successfully, people need to keep themselves on track."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":79,"advanced":"X widens the gap between Y and Z.","simple":"X increases the difference between Y and Z.","alternative":"Because of X, Y and Z become less equal."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":80,"advanced":"X places vulnerable groups at a disadvantage.","simple":"X makes life harder for people who are already at greater risk.","alternative":"People with fewer resources are more likely to be harmed by X."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":81,"advanced":"X promotes social mobility.","simple":"X helps people improve their economic or social position.","alternative":"X gives people a better chance to move to a higher level in society."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":82,"advanced":"X strengthens social cohesion.","simple":"X helps people in society feel more connected and cooperative.","alternative":"X can bring different groups together."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":83,"advanced":"X requires greater public accountability.","simple":"The people responsible for X should explain their decisions and be answerable for them.","alternative":"There needs to be a clearer way to hold decision makers responsible for X."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":84,"advanced":"X raises ethical concerns.","simple":"X creates questions about what is morally acceptable.","alternative":"People may worry that X is unfair or morally wrong."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":85,"advanced":"X should be subject to rigorous scrutiny.","simple":"X should be examined very carefully.","alternative":"Authorities should look closely at X before accepting or expanding it."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":86,"advanced":"X risks becoming a privilege rather than a right.","simple":"Only richer or more powerful people may be able to access X.","alternative":"If X becomes too expensive or restricted, ordinary people may be excluded."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":87,"advanced":"X can improve accessibility.","simple":"X can make a service easier for more people to reach or use.","alternative":"X can remove some of the barriers that stop people from accessing a service."},{"category":"Society and Public Policy","n":88,"advanced":"X needs a clear regulatory framework.","simple":"There should be clear rules explaining how X is allowed to operate.","alternative":"X needs proper laws and standards rather than vague guidance."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":89,"advanced":"Technology has lowered the barrier to entry.","simple":"Technology has made it easier for ordinary people to start doing something.","alternative":"People need less money, expertise, or equipment than before because of technology."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":90,"advanced":"Algorithms can create echo chambers.","simple":"Algorithms can repeatedly show people ideas they already agree with.","alternative":"People may end up seeing fewer opposing viewpoints because platforms personalise content."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":91,"advanced":"Technology can blur the boundary between work and personal life.","simple":"Technology can make it hard to know when work ends and free time begins.","alternative":"People may remain connected to work even after office hours."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":92,"advanced":"Automation can displace workers.","simple":"Machines or software can replace some jobs.","alternative":"Some workers may lose their roles when tasks become automated."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":93,"advanced":"Digital tools can democratise access to information.","simple":"Digital tools can make information available to many more people.","alternative":"People no longer need to live near major institutions to access knowledge."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":94,"advanced":"Convenience can come at the expense of privacy.","simple":"Services may become easier to use, but users may have to give up more personal data.","alternative":"People often trade some privacy for greater convenience."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":95,"advanced":"Misinformation can spread at an unprecedented pace.","simple":"False information can travel faster and reach more people than before.","alternative":"Online platforms can make inaccurate claims spread extremely quickly."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":96,"advanced":"Technology is a tool rather than an end in itself.","simple":"Technology should help achieve a goal; using it is not automatically valuable.","alternative":"The important question is what technology helps us do, not simply whether we use it."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":97,"advanced":"The digital divide can reinforce existing inequality.","simple":"Unequal access to technology can make social inequality worse.","alternative":"People without devices or internet access may fall further behind."},{"category":"Technology and Media","n":98,"advanced":"Constant connectivity can fragment attention.","simple":"Being connected all the time can make it harder to focus for long periods.","alternative":"Frequent notifications and messages can repeatedly break concentration."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":99,"advanced":"Education should equip people with transferable skills.","simple":"Education should teach skills that are useful in many jobs and situations.","alternative":"Students need abilities they can apply beyond one specific subject or career."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":100,"advanced":"Academic credentials do not necessarily reflect competence.","simple":"Having a degree does not always mean someone can perform well in practice.","alternative":"Qualifications and real ability are related, but they are not the same thing."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":101,"advanced":"Practical experience bridges the gap between theory and practice.","simple":"Real work experience helps people apply what they learned in books or classes.","alternative":"Experience shows how theoretical knowledge works in real situations."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":102,"advanced":"Job satisfaction is not solely determined by salary.","simple":"Money is only one factor that affects whether people enjoy their work.","alternative":"A high salary does not automatically make a job satisfying."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":103,"advanced":"Remote work offers greater autonomy but requires self-discipline.","simple":"Working from home gives people more control, but they need to manage themselves well.","alternative":"Remote workers have more freedom, but they must stay organised without constant supervision."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":104,"advanced":"Continuous learning is essential in a rapidly changing labour market.","simple":"People need to keep learning because job requirements change quickly.","alternative":"Skills can become outdated, so workers have to continue developing throughout their careers."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":105,"advanced":"Standardised tests capture only part of a student’s ability.","simple":"Tests measure some skills but cannot show everything a student can do.","alternative":"A single exam gives an incomplete picture of a person’s ability."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":106,"advanced":"Competition can be motivating up to a point.","simple":"Some competition can encourage effort, but too much can become stressful or harmful.","alternative":"Competition helps when it pushes people forward without overwhelming them."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":107,"advanced":"Specialisation can improve expertise but reduce flexibility.","simple":"Focusing deeply on one area can make someone highly skilled but less adaptable.","alternative":"Specialists may know one field very well but have fewer options if that field changes."},{"category":"Education and Work","n":108,"advanced":"A healthy work culture can improve retention.","simple":"People are more likely to stay in a company when the workplace is supportive and fair.","alternative":"A good working environment can reduce the number of employees who leave."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":109,"advanced":"Short-term economic gains can create long-term environmental costs.","simple":"A policy may make money now but cause environmental damage later.","alternative":"What helps the economy in the short run may create bigger ecological problems in the future."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":110,"advanced":"Individual action is necessary but insufficient.","simple":"Personal choices help, but they cannot solve the whole problem alone.","alternative":"People should change their behaviour, but governments and companies also need to act."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":111,"advanced":"The environmental cost is often externalised.","simple":"The person or company causing environmental harm does not always pay the full cost.","alternative":"Pollution can impose costs on society even when the producer avoids paying for the damage."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":112,"advanced":"Renewable energy can reduce dependence on finite resources.","simple":"Renewable energy can make countries less reliant on resources that will eventually run out.","alternative":"Using wind or solar power reduces the need for limited fuels such as coal and oil."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":113,"advanced":"Sustainable consumption requires changes in both supply and demand.","simple":"Businesses and consumers both need to change for consumption to become more sustainable.","alternative":"Producing greener goods is not enough unless people also choose them."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":114,"advanced":"Environmental policies can create distributional effects.","simple":"A green policy can affect rich and poor groups differently.","alternative":"The cost of environmental rules may fall more heavily on some groups than others."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":115,"advanced":"Prevention is preferable to irreversible damage.","simple":"It is better to stop serious environmental harm before it cannot be undone.","alternative":"Trying to fix the damage afterwards is far less reliable than stopping it from happening in the first place."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":116,"advanced":"Urban density can reduce per-capita resource use.","simple":"When people live closer together, each person may need less land, energy, or transport.","alternative":"Compact cities can use resources more efficiently per person."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":117,"advanced":"Consumer convenience often generates hidden environmental costs.","simple":"Easy and fast services can create pollution or waste that customers do not immediately see.","alternative":"Convenience may look cheap because some environmental costs are not included in the price."},{"category":"Environment and Sustainability","n":118,"advanced":"Long-term sustainability requires systemic change.","simple":"Small individual changes are not enough; the wider system also needs to change.","alternative":"Lasting environmental progress requires changes in infrastructure, rules, and incentives."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":119,"advanced":"It left a lasting impression on me.","simple":"I remembered it for a long time because it affected me strongly.","alternative":"It stayed in my mind long after it happened."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":120,"advanced":"It pushed me out of my comfort zone.","simple":"It made me do something unfamiliar or difficult.","alternative":"I had to deal with a situation I was not used to."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":121,"advanced":"It gave me a new perspective on X.","simple":"It changed the way I thought about X.","alternative":"After that experience, I saw X differently."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":122,"advanced":"I took it for granted at the time.","simple":"At the time, I did not fully appreciate how valuable it was.","alternative":"I only realised its value after I no longer had it."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":123,"advanced":"It was a steep learning curve.","simple":"I had to learn a lot in a short period of time.","alternative":"The beginning was difficult because there was so much to learn."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":124,"advanced":"I had mixed feelings about it.","simple":"I felt both positive and negative emotions about it.","alternative":"Part of me liked it, while another part did not."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":125,"advanced":"It did not live up to my expectations.","simple":"It was not as good as I expected.","alternative":"I expected much more, so I was disappointed."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":126,"advanced":"It exceeded my expectations.","simple":"It was much better than I thought it would be.","alternative":"I was surprised by how good it turned out to be."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":127,"advanced":"I gradually grew accustomed to it.","simple":"It felt strange at first, but it became normal over time.","alternative":"After some time, I got used to it."},{"category":"Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2","n":128,"advanced":"In hindsight, I would have handled it differently.","simple":"Looking back, I think I should have acted in another way.","alternative":"Now that I know the outcome, I would make a different choice."}],"logicCategories":["Cause and Effect","Benefits, Costs and Trade-offs","Comparison and Contrast","Opinion and Evaluation","Uncertainty, Probability and Evidence","Change and Trends","Problems and Solutions","People, Behaviour and Psychology","Society and Public Policy","Technology and Media","Education and Work","Environment and Sustainability","Personal Experience and Speaking Part 2"],"logicPrinciple":"Do not translate words. Translate the idea.","logicPrincipleDetail":"When an advanced phrase disappears from memory, reduce it to a basic logical relationship: cause, effect, comparison, trade-off, probability, change, problem, solution, behaviour, or evaluation. Then rebuild the sentence with ordinary words.","logicExampleAdvanced":"Social media can distort people’s perception of reality.","logicExampleSimple":"Social media can make people see the world in a way that is not completely realistic.","rescueFrames":[["Definition","It is basically a situation where... / It is the idea that..."],["Cause","X happens because... / One reason for X is..."],["Effect","Because of X, Y becomes... / X can lead to..."],["Trade-off","You gain X, but you give up some Y."],["Comparison","Compared with X, Y is... / The main difference is..."],["Uncertainty","There is a good chance that... / We cannot be completely sure that..."],["Evaluation","The main advantage/problem is... / I think this matters because..."],["Example","A simple example would be... / You can see this when..."],["Correction","What I mean is... / A better way to put it is..."],["Unknown word","I do not know the exact word for it, but it is basically..."]],"logicDrills":["One-Second Rule: if the exact word does not appear within one second, stop searching and explain the idea.","Ban-the-Word Drill: pick one advanced phrase from the book and explain it for 20 seconds without using any key word from the original phrase.","Two-Level Drill: say the sophisticated sentence, then immediately say the same idea as if speaking to a 10-year-old.","Compression Drill: take a long explanation and reduce it to one clear sentence.","Expansion Drill: take one abstract word and explain it with cause + consequence + example.","Part 3 Drill: answer a question for 60 seconds and deliberately paraphrase your central idea twice without repeating the original wording.","Part 2 Rescue Drill: tell a story for two minutes; every time you forget a word, describe function, appearance, cause, effect, or example instead of pausing.","Writing Precision Drill: replace vague words such as good, bad, big, and important only when a more precise word genuinely improves meaning."]};
